    body: "Musical notation is a system for writing down music so it can be read and played by others, even if they've never heard the piece before. A time signature, written at the start of a piece, tells musicians how many beats are in each bar — in 4/4 time, there are 4 beats per bar.\n\nInstruments are grouped into families based on how they produce sound. The brass family, including instruments like the trumpet, produces sound through vibrating lips against a mouthpiece. The woodwind family, including instruments like the flute, produces sound by blowing air across or through an opening.\n\nComposing a simple rhythm means creating your own original pattern of beats and sounds, rather than only playing music written by someone else.\n\nUnderstanding notation, instrument families, and composition gives musicians the tools to both read existing music and create their own.",
